HTML=r'''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Experiment recordings</title>
<style>
:root{color-scheme:dark;font:14px system-ui;background:#111820;color:#e8edf2}body{margin:16px;min-width:760px}button,input,select{font:inherit}button,select{background:#253340;color:inherit;border:1px solid #526273;border-radius:4px;padding:5px}header{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:36px}#run-heading{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0;max-width:40vw}#run-heading strong{overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}#run-heading code{font-size:11px;color:#9fb3c4}#browser{border:1px solid #3c4d5b;border-radius:6px;background:#151f28;padding:8px;margin-top:8px}#browser[hidden]{display:none}.browser-bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:center}#run-search{width:300px;padding:5px;background:#17212b;color:inherit;border:1px solid #526273;border-radius:4px}#comparison-filter{max-width:420px}#run-count{font-size:12px;color:#bac8d5}#catalog-error{font-size:12px;color:#edc37e}#tag-filters{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:3px;margin:8px 0;max-height:190px;overflow-y:auto}.tag-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px;align-items:center}.tag-category{font-size:11px;color:#9fb3c4;width:88px}.chip{font-size:11px;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:10px;background:#1d2a35;border-color:#43566a}.chip[aria-pressed=true]{background:#2f5878;border-color:#7dc8ff}#run-list{max-height:260px;overflow-y:auto;border-top:1px solid #293847}.run-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:128px minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,300px) 90px;gap:10px;width:100%;text-align:left;background:transparent;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid #22303c;border-radius:0;padding:4px 6px;font-size:12px}.run-row[aria-pressed=true]{background:#304960}.run-row time,.run-row code{color:#9fb3c4;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}.run-name{overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}.run-status[data-status=running]{color:#85ce98}.run-status[data-status=failed],.run-status[data-status=blocked]{color:#ed8b9a}#compared{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;margin-top:8px;font-size:12px}.compared{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px;align-items:center}.env-app{display:grid;grid-template-columns:300px minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px;margin-top:12px}.env-list{border:1px solid #3c4d5b;border-radius:6px;background:#151f28;display:flex;flex-direction:column;max-height:calc(100vh - 110px)}.env-list-bar{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #293847}#environment-list{overflow-y:auto}.env-row{display:block;width:100%;text-align:left;background:transparent;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid #22303c;border-radius:0;padding:6px 8px;font-size:12px}.env-row[aria-pressed=true]{background:#304960}.env-row small{display:block;color:#9fb3c4;margin-top:2px}.env-stage .physics-frame{height:calc(100vh - 150px);min-height:480px}.env-prompt{margin-top:12px}.env-prompt-body{padding:8px 12px;font-size:12px}.env-prompt pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:12px;line-height:1.45;background:#0d141a;border:1px solid #293847;border-radius:4px;padding:8px;margin:6px 0}.env-mode #browser,.env-mode #browse-toggle,.env-mode #run-heading,.env-mode #compared,.env-mode #model-context,.env-mode #execution-mode,.env-mode #status,.env-mode #live-label,.env-mode #refresh{display:none!important}#server-life{margin-left:auto;font-size:12px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;border:1px solid #677989;border-radius:3px;padding:3px 6px;white-space:nowrap}#server-life.low{border-color:#e0a050;color:#f3c87a}#execution-mode{font-size:11px;border:1px solid #677989;border-radius:3px;padding:3px 5px;white-space:nowrap}#status{color:#bac8d5;font-size:12px}.windows{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin-top:12px}.window{border:1px solid #3c4d5b;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden}.caption{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:7px 10px;background:#1c2832}.stage{height:280px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:#080c10;position:relative}.stage img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain}.empty{position:absolute;color:#b8c4d0;padding:20px}.recording-range{width:calc(100% - 20px);margin:10px}.timebar{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:center;margin:12px 0}#timeline{flex:1}#clock{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;min-width:150px}#warning{color:#edc37e;font-size:12px;white-space:pre-wrap}#progress{height:176px;overflow-y:auto;border:1px solid #3c4d5b;border-radius:5px;background:#151f28}#progress button{display:block;width:100%;text-align:left;background:transparent;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid #293847;border-radius:0;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.4;padding:8px 12px}#progress button.selected{background:#304960;border-left:3px solid #7dc8ff}#progress button time{color:#9fcbeb;margin-right:12px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.label{font-size:12px;color:#b5c5d4;margin:10px 0 6px}#metric-choices{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 16px;margin:8px 0;max-height:140px;overflow:auto}#metric-choices label{font-size:12px}.legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 12px;font-size:11px;max-height:120px;overflow:auto}.legend label{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;cursor:pointer}.legend input{margin:0;accent-color:currentColor}.legend label:has(input:not(:checked)){opacity:.55}.overlay{position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none}.overlay svg{height:100%;width:100%;cursor:default}.stage img[hidden]{display:none}#plots{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px;max-height:520px;overflow-y:auto}article{border:1px solid #3c4d5b;border-radius:5px;background:#17212b;min-width:0;padding:8px}article h3{font-size:12px;margin:0 0 3px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}svg{display:block;width:100%;height:160px;touch-action:none;cursor:crosshair}svg text{font:10px system-ui;fill:#bac8d5}.cursor{stroke:#f6ce73;stroke-width:1.3;stroke-dasharray:5 4;pointer-events:none}.axis{stroke:#506273;stroke-width:1}.metric{stroke:#7ac7ed;stroke-width:1.8;fill:none}.point{fill:#7ac7ed}#filter{width:340px;padding:5px;background:#17212b;color:inherit;border:1px solid #526273;border-radius:4px}details{margin-top:12px;font-size:12px;color:#bac8d5}a{color:#8bcfff}#videos a{display:inline-block;margin:5px 15px 5px 0}.footer{font-size:11px;color:#92a5b5;margin-top:10px}.tabs{display:flex;gap:4px}.tabs button[aria-selected=true]{background:#304960;border-color:#7dc8ff}.physics-frame{display:block;width:100%;height:480px;border:0;background:#080c10}.physics-controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin:8px 0}#physics-unavailable{border:1px solid #8a6d3b;background:#2a2316;color:#f0d9a8;border-radius:5px;padding:10px 12px;margin-top:12px;white-space:pre-wrap}#version-label{font-size:12px;color:#d6e2ec;min-height:18px}#version-ticks button{position:absolute;top:0;width:9px;height:14px;padding:0;transform:translateX(-50%);border-radius:2px}
</style></head><body>
<header><button type="button" id="browse-toggle" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="browser">Runs ▾</button><div id="run-heading"><strong id="run-title">No run selected</strong><code id="run-directory"></code></div><nav class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Dashboard view"><button type="button" id="view-recordings" role="tab" aria-selected="true">Recordings</button><button type="button" id="view-physics" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Interactive physics</button><button type="button" id="view-environments" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Environments</button></nav><span id="execution-mode"></span><span id="status"></span><label id="live-label" title="Poll the server for new runs and for new records of an active run"><input type="checkbox" id="live" checked> Live</label><button type="button" id="refresh">Refresh</button><span id="server-life" hidden title="Time left before the dashboard server's Slurm job ends"></span></header>
<section id="browser" aria-label="Run browser"><div class="browser-bar"><input id="run-search" type="search" placeholder="Search name, run ID or factor" aria-label="Search runs"><label>Sort <select id="run-sort" aria-label="Sort runs"><option value="date-desc">Newest first</option><option value="date-asc">Oldest first</option><option value="name-asc">Name A–Z</option><option value="name-desc">Name Z–A</option></select></label><label>Experiment <select id="comparison-filter" aria-label="Experiment comparison"></select></label><button type="button" id="clear-filters">Clear filters</button><span id="run-count"></span><span id="catalog-error"></span></div><div id="tag-filters" aria-label="Tag filters"></div><div id="run-list" role="listbox" aria-label="Runs"></div></section>
<div id="compared" aria-label="Experiments containing this run"></div>
<details id="model-context"><summary>Model task, permitted access and record limitations</summary><div id="researcher-notes" style="white-space:pre-wrap"></div><pre id="model-context-text" style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></pre></details>
<div id="recordings-view">
<div class="windows">
<section class="window" data-world="reference"><div class="caption"><strong>Reference</strong><span id="reference-meta"></span></div><div class="stage"><div class="overlay" id="reference-overlay"></div><img id="reference-frame" alt="Recorded reference camera" hidden><div id="reference-empty" class="empty">No recorded frames</div></div><input id="reference-timeline" class="recording-range" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.001" value="0" aria-label="Reference recording wall time"></section>
<section class="window" data-world="candidate"><div class="caption"><strong>Reconstructed</strong><span id="candidate-meta"></span></div><div class="stage"><div class="overlay" id="candidate-overlay"></div><img id="candidate-frame" alt="Recorded reconstructed camera" hidden><div id="candidate-empty" class="empty">No recorded frames</div></div><input id="candidate-timeline" class="recording-range" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.001" value="0" aria-label="Reconstructed recording wall time"></section>
</div>
<div class="timebar"><button id="play">Play wall time</button><div id="timeline-column" style="flex:1;min-width:0"><input id="timeline" style="display:block;width:100%;margin:0" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.001" value="0" aria-label="Shared wall timeline"><div id="action-ticks" aria-label="Recorded world action markers" style="position:relative;height:48px;margin:0 8px"></div></div><label>Speed <select id="playback-speed" aria-label="Playback speed"><option value="1">1×</option><option value="2">2×</option><option value="4">4×</option><option value="8">8×</option><option value="16">16×</option></select></label><output id="clock">0.000 s / 0.000 s</output></div>
<div style="font-size:11px"><span style="color:#7ac7ed">● Reference actions</span> · <span style="color:#f1ba67">● Reconstruction actions</span> · <span style="color:#ae94ed">● Meta actions</span> · click a marker to reveal its log entry</div>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="grasp-overlay" checked> Show grasp point and recorded handle trajectory</label><div id="warning"></div>
<div class="label">Event log · click a line to seek · scrolling only scrolls</div><label>Log type <select id="log-filter" aria-label="Log type"><option value="all">All</option><option value="model">Model progress</option><option value="reference">Reference actions</option><option value="candidate">Reconstruction actions</option><option value="meta">Meta actions</option><option value="provider">Provider summaries</option></select></label><section id="progress" aria-label="Timestamped event log"></section>
<div class="label">Selected metrics · shared plots for comparable curves · gaps mean NaN / unavailable</div><input id="filter" placeholder="Filter metric names" aria-label="Filter metric names"><div id="metric-choices" aria-label="Metric checklist"></div><section id="plots"></section><div id="candidate-unavailable" style="white-space:pre-wrap"></div>
<details><summary>Verified original recordings and snapshot metadata</summary><div id="videos"></div><pre id="snapshot"></pre><pre id="candidate-history" style="white-space:pre-wrap"></pre></details>
<div class="footer">Wall-clock playback holds each world’s latest recorded frame while it is idle. Simulation times and reset episodes are not aligned to one another. Original MP4 downloads retain encoded timing; synchronized playback above uses exact timestamped camera frames.</div>
</div>
<section id="physics-view" hidden aria-label="Interactive physics">
<div id="physics-unavailable" hidden></div>
<div class="windows">
<section class="window"><div class="caption"><strong>Reference · source scene</strong><span id="physics-reference-meta"></span></div><iframe id="physics-reference" class="physics-frame" title="Interactive reference physics"></iframe></section>
<section class="window"><div class="caption"><strong>Reconstructed · selected version</strong><span id="physics-candidate-meta"></span></div><iframe id="physics-candidate" class="physics-frame" title="Interactive reconstruction physics"></iframe></section>
</div>
<div class="timebar"><button type="button" id="version-previous" aria-label="Previous recorded version">◀</button><div style="flex:1;min-width:0"><input id="version-timeline" style="display:block;width:100%;margin:0" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.001" value="0" aria-label="World-model version by wall time"><div id="version-ticks" aria-label="Recorded world-model versions" style="position:relative;height:18px;margin:0 8px"></div></div><button type="button" id="version-next" aria-label="Next recorded version">▶</button><output id="version-clock">0.000 s</output></div>
<div style="font-size:11px"><span style="color:#f1ba67">● Candidate load</span> · <span style="color:#ae94ed">● Submission</span> · <span style="color:#8a98a6">● Archive unavailable</span> · the scrubber selects the latest version loaded by that wall time</div>
<div id="version-label"></div>
<div class="physics-controls"><button type="button" data-physics="reset">Reset both</button><button type="button" data-physics="play">Play both</button><button type="button" data-physics="pause">Pause both</button><button type="button" data-physics="step">Step both 0.1 s</button><label><input type="checkbox" id="physics-sync" checked> Synchronize cameras</label><label title="Pick a part in each world; one drag then moves both grasp handles by the same displacement"><input type="checkbox" id="physics-couple"> Coupled grasp</label><span id="couple-status"></span></div>
<section class="window" id="overlay-window" hidden><div class="caption"><strong>Overlay · reference opaque, reconstruction translucent</strong><span>click a part of either world to pick it</span></div><iframe id="physics-overlay" class="physics-frame" title="Overlay of reference and reconstruction physics"></iframe></section>
<div id="physics-status" class="footer"></div>
<div class="footer">The viewers run live MuJoCo on the inspector's Slurm test node. Click a movable body to attach the benchmark's ideal point grasp at that surface point, then drag the gizmo; the handle follows at a bounded speed and imposes no orientation. Each world simulates independently from its own initial state; the reference is the private source scene. With <b>Coupled grasp</b>, pick the corresponding part in each world (in its own viewer or in the overlay). Both worlds hold paused until both parts are picked, then play together; dragging any gizmo moves both handles by the same displacement from their own grasp points, and playback controls act on both. Part correspondence is your choice; none is inferred. Versions are recovered from the verified audit: successful candidate loads and distinct submissions only. Edits that were never loaded are unavailable.</div>
</section>
<section id="environments-view" hidden aria-label="Environments">
<div id="environment-unavailable" hidden></div>
<div class="env-app"><aside class="env-list" aria-label="Environment list"><div class="env-list-bar"><strong>Environments</strong><label>Sort <select id="environment-sort" aria-label="Sort environments"><option value="built-desc">Newest built</option><option value="built-asc">Oldest built</option><option value="name-asc">Name A–Z</option></select></label></div><div id="environment-list" role="listbox" aria-label="Environments"></div></aside>
<section class="window env-stage"><div class="caption"><strong id="environment-title">Pick an environment</strong><span id="environment-meta"></span></div><iframe id="environment-frame" class="physics-frame" title="Interactive environment"></iframe></section></div>
<section class="window env-prompt"><div class="caption"><strong>Base prompt given to the agent</strong><span id="environment-prompt-meta"></span></div><div class="env-prompt-body"><div class="label">Task, exactly as the agent receives it</div><pre id="environment-task">Pick an environment.</pre><div id="environment-level" class="footer" hidden></div><details><summary>System prompt (identical for every environment)</summary><pre id="environment-system"></pre></details><div class="footer">Base condition: the current stop-when-done task and this robot family's model constraints, without per-experiment additions (named hinge parameters, stated masses, tool recommendations, "match every angle"). Read from <code>experiments/configs/generate-waves.py</code> and <code>examples/sandbox_agent.py</code>. The first message also carries the controller contract (permitted actions and observations for the run's sensing setup) and the first observation, which depend on the run, not the environment.</div></div></section>
<div class="footer">Live MuJoCo from the environment's authored initial state, on the inspector's Slurm test node. Click a movable object to attach the ideal point grasp at that surface point, then drag the gizmo; Play, Pause, Step, Reset, Release and speed are in the viewer's side panel. These are the authored scenes under <code>environments/</code>; each run's perturbed copy (hard physics, recoloring) is in that run's Interactive physics view. "Built" is when the scene's own files last changed.</div>
</section>
<script src="catalog.js"></script><script src="dashboard.js"></script></body></html>'''

